administration, helping stabilize the monarchy after a major war.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-11T11:15:33Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#34592972894", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Count Karl Ferdinand von Königsegg-Erps was an administrator and diplomat in Habsburg service.", "newValue": "Count Karl Ferdinand von Königsegg-Erps (1696–1759) emerged as a pivotal figure in 18th-century Habsburg diplomacy and administration, serving as Imperial Vice-Chancellor and a key negotiator during the tumultuous War of the Austrian Succession. His career underscored the intricate balance of power politics and dynastic succession that defined the Early Modern European landscape, positioning him as a central architect of Austrian foreign policy under Empress Maria Theresa and an influential voice in the Holy Roman Empire's chancery.

