nse challenge. His diplomatic efforts secured crucial alliances and resources, directly impacting the outcome of the War of the Austrian Succession and the survival of Maria Theresa's inheritance.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-11T11:16:05Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#34592972894", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Count Karl Ferdinand von Königsegg-Erps was an administrator and diplomat in Habsburg service.", "newValue": "Count Charles Ferdinand of Königsegg-Erps (1696–1759) was a preeminent Habsburg statesman and diplomat whose career spanned the reigns of Emperor Charles VI and Empress Maria Theresa. Born into the influential Swabian noble house of Königsegg-Erps in Vienna, his lineage provided him access to the highest echelons of Imperial service. His diplomatic acumen and administrative skill were critical in navigating the complex geopolitical landscape of 18th-century Europe, particularly during the tumultuous War of the Austrian Succession, where he worked to secure alliances and maintain the integrity of the Habsburg dominions.

